Note = {International Conference on Urban Climatology (ICUC 96), ESSEN, GERMANY,
   JUN   10, 1996-JUN 14, 1997},
Abstract = {The intensification of an urban heat island, and its influence on the
   seasonal and annual air temperature measurements of the
   Prague-Klementinum station, is studied through a comparison with rural
   stations. Urban warming in the period from 1922 to 1995 was most
   conspicuous in winter and in spring (0.06 degrees C 10 yr(-1)), and the
   smallest and least significant in summer (0.01 degrees C 10 yr(-1)).
   Since the 1960s, a stagnation in the development of the urban heat
   island has appeared. The degree of urban warming prior to 1922 can only
   be roughly determined because of the lack of a suitable set of
   homogeneous reference stations. The results of this study are compared
   with other studies analogous in character. (C) 1999 Elsevier Science
   Ltd. All rights reserved.},
