   SICAP: COGNITIVE CHARACTERISTICS OF TRANSDISCIPLINARITY. APPLICATIONS IN
   PSYCHOLOGY AND PSYCHOTHERAPIES},
Year = {2017},
Pages = {96-101},
Note = {24th International Symposium on Research and Applications in Psychology
   (SICAP) - Cognitive Characteristics of Transdisciplinarity. Applications
   in Psychology and Psychotherapies, Timisoara, ROMANIA, MAR 24-26, 2017},
Abstract = {This study was meant to explore the correlation between the positive and
   negative affectivity (namely, positive and negative emotions) and the
   level of sales performance, in a commercial campus from Bucharest,
   Romania ({''}Aleea Castanilor{''}).
   The sample was composed of 30 participants of which 21 female gender and
   (male gender, aged between 20 and 70 years old. Data was collected via
   survey questionnaires, PANAS - X for the measurement of the positive and
   negative affectivity and a check section with 6 intervals that described
   the number of items sold on average per month, for the measurement of
   the level of sales performance.
   Results indicate a positive correlation between positive affectivity and
   the level of sales performance, fact that confirmed the study
   hypothesis, considering the fact that the higher the level of positive
   affectivity is, the more the level of sales performance increases and
   the higher the level of the negative affectivity is, the more the level
   of sales performance decreases.},
