   Creative Thinking in Engineering and Academic Education, Sibiu, ROMANIA,
   JUN 02-05, 2011},
Organization = {Lucian Blaga Univ Sibiu, Mfg Sci Dept, Teachers Training Dept, Fac Engn},
Abstract = {This paper explores the perceptions of second year university students
   of their group work project, in a Theory and Methodology of Instruction
   Course. Small groups were required to research, analyze and deliver
   presentations regarding specific syllabus-based topics. A survey
   questionnaire at the end of the project captured their perceptions on
   group work activities. Analysis of responses from questionnaire revealed
   that the group project was a positive learning experience for most of
   the students. Students reported improvements in different skills,
   important not only for the academic purpose, but also for their future
   undertaking. The difficulties the students encountered during the whole
   process and their suggestions for improvement of group work experience
   are also presented.},
