Organization = {Malaysian Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {As the world battles with measures of finding a lasting solution to the
   problem of climate change, this study examines the perception and
   attitude of education students. This group was purposely chosen by the
   author because she believes that these respondents will become future
   educators who will be the molder of the youth in the future and they
   will also be the future citizens who will be facing the enormous impacts
   of climate change in the future. Analyses of data revealed that
   respondents have high perception and attitude on climate change and
   there is no significant difference in their perception and attitude
   towards climate change when grouped according to age and sex. This only
   means that regardless of age and sex, the respondents have the same
   perception and attitude towards climate change. Furthermore, there is a
   significant relationship between the perception and attitude of the
   students on climate change which implies that the higher the perception
   and awareness of the respondents on climate change, the more positive
   their attitude on climate change will be.},
