   Metropolitan Area},
Booktitle = {DYNAMICS OF URBAN AGGLOMERATION IN CHINA: PREFERENCES OF ENERGY-SAVING
   AND ENVIRONMENT-FRIENDLY SOCIETY},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {202-208},
Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Wuhan metropolitan area is now on the fast track of both
   industrialization and urbanization, and the `resource-saving and
   environment-friendly' social development serves as a precious
   opportunity as well as a tense challenge. For one thing, it can make the
   best use of the core post and impact of Wuhan, the only
   ultra-metropolitan city in central china. For another, it can also
   prompt the reform of Wuhan metropolitan area, which will thereafter
   stimulate the development of Hubei province, even the development of
   whole central china, thus the uprising of central china can be realized.
   From the perspective of philosophical basis and sustainable development
   theory of `resource-saving and environment-friendly' social development,
   the thesis points out the shortcomings lying in current `resource-saving
   and environment-friendly' social development and puts forward relevant
   constructive suggestions, through a thorough analysis of current
   `resource-saving and environment-friendly' situations of Wuhan
   metropolitan area, ranging from economical development, technological
   innovation, to consuming mode, and ecological protection.},
