Note = {Conference of the
   International-Society-for-Environmental-Information-Sciences on
   Environmental Informatics, Xiamen, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 26-28, 2005},
Organization = {Xiamen Univ; Ryerson Univ; Int Soc Environm Informat Sci},
Abstract = {Ecological Footprint (EF) is a new. indicator to quantify the
   sustainability. EF is defined as an ecologically productive land area
   which could sustain and support a certain population under an acceptable
   lifestyle. Application of this concept to urban ecosystem can
   quantitatively assess the stress and impact on natural ecosystem from
   urban economic activities, and thus health condition of urban ecosystem
   can be examined. This paper presents a comprehensive framework on urban
   EF calculation and its application to the City of Guangzhou, Guangdong
   province of China. The variation of EF in the past 5 years was analyzed.
   The results show that the City of Guangzhou had an EF of 2.5 ha/cap and
   a carrying capacity of 0.2 ha/cap in the year of 2000, respectively.
   During the period of 1995 to 2000 the EF per GDP tends to decrease while
   the EF per cap tends to increase. The results indicate that the economic
   development in Guangzhou is facing increased stress and challenge, and
   the municipal authorities should focus on improving efficiencies of
   resources development and utilization,, promoting resources-saving
   initiatives, and lessening ecological footprints in the future
   ecological construction. These measures will help the City of Guangzhou
   move toward an ecologically sound city.},
