Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers Geoscience
   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {Disasters such as earthquakes, hurricanes, and flooding are responsible
   for large-scale infrastructure damages and loss of human lives.
   Immediately after disaster strikes, one of the most critical and
   difficult tasks is accurately assessing the extent and severity of the
   disaster. This task is especially challenging in areas isolated by the
   disaster; in such cases, remote sensing information provides the best
   alternative to tackle this problem. This paper presents a damage mapping
   framework using remote sensing imagery acquired from previous disasters.
   The proposed deep learning-based framework is trained to learn features
   related to building damage using imagery from previous disasters that
   were collected from different regions around the world. Then, it is
   tested to recognize damage from a different urban environment.},
