Note = {2nd International Conference on Sustainable Development of Water and
   Environment (ICSDWE), Hong Kong, HONG KONG, JAN 22-23, 2019},
Abstract = {Being different from the traditional analysis of urban expansion in
   Shanghai from the perspective of humanities or urban geography, this
   study applies the Remote Sensing (RS) and Geographical Information
   System (GIS) spatial information technologies to analyze the
   spatio-temporal characteristics and evolution of urban land expansion in
   Shanghai's urbanization process. It provides a basis for further
   research on the mechanism of urbanization process. In this study, we
   processed and analyzed the multi-temporal remote sensing images (Landsat
   series) in Shanghai from 1995 to 2016. A multidimensional feature space
   was constructed. Then the image classification was carried out by the
   support vector machine (SVM). On the basis of classification results,
   the central city zone was extracted by method of regional connectivity.
   After analyzing the change of area, center of gravity, location and
   spatial distribution of the central city zone, the spatial layout and
   trend of urban expansion are obtained. Finally, the driving force of
   urban expansion in Shanghai is analyzed. The analysis results accurately
   reflect the process of Shanghai's urban expansion.},
