Year = {2024},
Pages = {239-245},
Note = {2024 International Conference on Energy and Environment-ICEE-Bringing
   together Engineering and Economics, Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, JUN 06-07, 2024},
Abstract = {City certifications are considered quality indicators, as they take on
   the status of smart, sustainable, or resilient, for example. Therefore,
   the objective of this research is to analyze the relationships between
   Brazilian indicators and the objective of certification of recognized
   cities in the year 2023, as a response to better indicators of
   sustainability, urban well-being, and social inequality. This is an
   exploratory documentary research that uses comparative and statistical
   methods, predominantly quantitative, from public secondary data.
   Initially, Brazilian cities recognized in the year 2023 were searched
   for, later the HDI, GINI, IDSC, and IBEU indicators were selected, built
   a tabular database of cities x characterization| Certifications. The
   information was statistically analyzed by two-dimensional analysis,
   evaluating the qualitative and quantitative relationships between the
   Brazilian indicators and the certification objective. The analysis
   showed the sociospatial inequality between the Brazilian regions and the
   certified cities, a tendency towards medium sustainability, and
   deficiencies related to the provision of services and urban
   infrastructure. It was also found that although the MHDI of the
   certified cities is predominantly high, this did not improve the aspect
   of income inequality. It was concluded that the certified cities have
   deficiencies in the areas of sustainability and urban well-being, like
   the set of Brazilian cities.},
