Organization = {Univ Sci \& Technol Beijing; Water \& Wastewater Engn Magazine
   Publishing; Univ Appl Sci Stuttgart; Tech Univ Hamburg, Harburg;
   Stockholm Environm Inst; China Node Sustainable Sanitat; Beijing Environ
   Syst Co},
Abstract = {Retention soil filters become more and more very important tools in
   sustainable infrastructure urban planning. They are ecologically
   important mechanical-biological rainwater treatment units with detention
   functions. They are usable for all kinds of development measures in
   urban and rural areas. They need more space, however, the total sewage
   treatment capacity and its ecological significance is much better
   compared to the traditionally used rainwater treatment processes. The
   cleaning capacity corresponds to precipitation and filtration or
   precipitation and flotation. In view of water quality improvement,
   erosion control, drift prevention and discharge infiltration and/or
   hydraulic stress prevention ground filters can be regarded as
   multifunction systems.
   Retention ground/soil filters are most important as an ecological
   compensation measure. They are to be regarded as landscaping elements
   and are as such easily integrated into the environment.},
