   for Sustainable Urban Development, Cardiff, WALES, SEP 15-16, 2005},
Abstract = {The concept of sustainability is becoming familiar and has already led
   to many initiatives of different types to put the concept into practice.
   There is a range of approaches, existing tools and methods that focus on
   the challenge of sustainability of European urban infrastructure. The
   actual problem is the transfer of knowledge to practice, the suggestion
   of ways of action and the integration of information. The Practical
   Evaluation Tool for Urban Sustainability (PETUS) research outcomes are
   presented here, on one side, as reflections upon these topics, and on
   the other side, as an operational framework developed with these
   objectives.},
