Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; WIT Transact Ecol \& Environm; Univ Alicante, Inst
   Water \& Environm Sci; Minist Educ \& Ciencia; Inst Agua \& Ciencias
   Ambientales; Patronato Municipal Turismo Alicante; Univ Alicante, Grupo
   Invest Modelizac Matemat Sistemas},
Abstract = {Shrimptons Creek is a small catchment in the suburban-commercial area of
   North Ryde, New South Wales, Australia. The original channel system was
   significantly modified by firstly agricultural, then suburban, and
   finally commercial development in its catchment and along the channel.
   Sewer lines, uncontrolled stormwater outlets, major road systems with
   culverts and significant weed infestation occurred over a period of more
   than 150 years. The opportunity was provided to rehabilitate a section
   of the channel and monitor the effectiveness of the rehabilitation. It
   is concluded that the rehabilitation impacted on the aesthetic amenity
   of the channel and had some limited effects on water quality. However,
   the failure to maintain the system, a problem identified elsewhere by
   the authors, has reduced the effectiveness of the rehabilitation.},
