   Engineering (ICCAHE 2013), Zhuhai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 27-28, 2013},
Abstract = {There have made great progress in urban space research which based on
   the individual bodily difference in the context of postmodernism.
   Feminine space also has been focused in the Architecture. In China,
   women often are regarded as one unit of sub-groups, whose living
   condition and living space had undergone great changes. Based on the
   bodily difference, from the view of functional requirements, behavior
   needs, physical needs and psychological requirements of women, the paper
   discusses the major existing problems in four aspects, which concluding
   function layout, transport supply, service facilities and space
   identify. Combined architecture and geography, sociology, urban
   planning, the paper uses the method of cognitive map and preference
   method to explore feminine cognitive pattern and behavior model, thus
   construct the ideal paradigm of urban feminine public space.},
