   Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 02-05, 2009},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol; Donghua Univ; Key Lab
   Explos Sci \& Technol},
Abstract = {For the purpose of relieving the double pressures of rapid urbanization
   and ecological protection of Harbin City in Northeast China and
   realizing urban ecological security, the staged characteristics and the
   ecological environmental effects of urban land use extension were
   analyzed, the evaluation indicator system was established including four
   subsystems and 19 specific indicators, the urban ecological security
   index was calculated and the situation of ecological security of Harbin
   City was evaluated by using the model of comprehensive evaluation. The
   results show that the comprehensive index of urban ecological security
   in Harbin City presents an uptrend overall, and the index ascended from
   0.165 in 1996 to 0.743 in 2006, so the ecological security has been up
   to scratch. However, the level in each subsystem was in the general and
   a little poor grade before 2004, but after 2004, all subsystems apart
   from urban environment were in above good grade after adjusted and
   optimized, only the environmental problems brought by rapid development
   in previous period were rather severe still.},
