Abstract = {This research chooses Shenzhen as the sample area and makes a
   comprehensive assessment of urban vulnerability by using an advanced
   tool named the Integrated Environmental Assessment Process at city-level
   of China. The assessment is composed of two parts, including: (1)
   assessing the two aspects of urban vulnerability comprehensively based
   on the analysis of status and origin of villages-in-city under the
   Driver-Pressure-State-Impact-Response (DPSIR) framework; (2) proposing
   an action plan to cope with urban vulnerability under the present policy
   framework. According to the case study of rapid urbanization process,
   the author finds that urban vulnerability in the rapid urbanization
   areas contains two aspects: one is the regional frangibility resulted
   from the existence of a large number of villages-in-city, the other one
   is the vulnerability of low-income groups who live in villages-in-city.},
