Abstract = {The interaction of people with physical spaces happens in reciprocal
   association, where the person-environment system is influenced by and
   causes an impact on human behavior. Bearing this in mind, this paper
   sets out to show how elderly residents perceive the environment in
   collective housing. What is therefore sought is to understand how the
   elderly perceive their space, in response to their wants and
   expectations, by applying different techniques for assessing perception
   in groups of elderly people. The findings in three institutions, in
   which elderly people reside, have shown a similarity in results, which
   are seen to be less than enlightening, probably due to the cognitive
   impairment of the elderly. (C) 2015 The Authors. Published by Elsevier
