Abstract = {One of the main pillars of tourism industry is the accommodation sector
   with its obvious environmental impact. This is the justification for the
   present study in quest for a sustainable tourism destination, which is
   the city of Mashhad. Being a magnet for pilgrimage tourism and
   non-pilgrimage holidaymaking, the political economy of this urban
   landscape is intertwined with tourism in one hand, and its future
   sustainability, onthe other. To achieve both sustainability and business
   success in this sector, hotels are responsible to invest on means
   andmeasures of internalizing environmental costs in short-term and to
